436 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 237 0 R
/T (My contribution for this project was the brainstorming of ideas for design, concept and theme. The website is also made for my brand in crocheting. I found this activity to be a brain teaser, it challenged critical thinking and careful planning. Although the coding was purely left to one of our members, I still understood how complex the process of making this was. There is a lot to be accounted for when making a website, the functionality of the whole user interface along with the aesthetic and appeal of it, the User Interface \(UI\) should be understandable and simple enough that it does not lead the users to be confused or lost when navigating through the website. It is hard for me to say that I enjoyed this project because of how complex it was, but that is only for my opinion because I do not enjoy coding as much as I thought I would. All things considered this was a brain teasing activity that challenges the brain to think more, and we all need that to strengthen our critical capacity. The project or even the subject as a whole does remind me of my 10th grade projects where we have to use block coding to make apps and such. The activities challenged me and made me study in advance, this impressed my teacher and classmates because of how far ahead I was. I underestimated the complexity of coding from scratch, but I do wish I can get that drive back again to excel in this kind of subject as I do enjoy making something and watching it work in the most intricate of ways. Coding is a like art in way but with more number and technical aspects, so it is fun to produce something and watching it do its thing. It is like staring at art and observing the emotion or the work put in to it.)
/E (My contribution for this project was the brainstorming of ideas for design, concept and theme. The website is also made for my brand in crocheting. I found this activity to be a brain teaser, it challenged critical thinking and careful planning. Although the coding was purely left to one of our members, I still understood how complex the process of making this was. There is a lot to be accounted for when making a website, the functionality of the whole user interface along with the aesthetic and appeal of it, the User Interface \(UI\) should be understandable and simple enough that it does not lead the users to be confused or lost when navigating through the website. It is hard for me to say that I enjoyed this project because of how complex it was, but that is only for my opinion because I do not enjoy coding as much as I thought I would. All things considered this was a brain teasing activity that challenges the brain to think more, and we all need that to strengthen our critical capacity. The project or even the subject as a whole does remind me of my 10th grade projects where we have to use block coding to make apps and such. The activities challenged me and made me study in advance, this impressed my teacher and classmates because of how far ahead I was. I underestimated the complexity of coding from scratch, but I do wish I can get that drive back again to excel in this kind of subject as I do enjoy making something and watching it work in the most intricate of ways. Coding is a like art in way but with more number and technical aspects, so it is fun to produce something and watching it do its thing. It is like staring at art and observing the emotion or the work put in to it.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
